  "runtimeCommit": "22b845afe1fe16bfa4821804d528f469366e4f8c",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nA minimum wage earner is not required to file an income tax return as they are exempt from income tax on their taxable income. This exemption includes holiday pay, overtime pay, night shift differential pay, and hazard pay.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practical terms, minimum wage earners can focus on their work without the burden of filing an income tax return, as their income falls below the taxable threshold. This exemption is designed to alleviate the financial burden on low-income workers, allowing them to retain their full earnings without the obligation of tax compliance.",
